# Succumb to the Cold's "one or two target creatures an opponent controls": three creatures an opponent controls are available and a
# fourth that Bot1 controls. Naming all three is refused (at most two), Bot1's own Ornithopter is refused (an opponent's only), and
# naming two taps both and puts a stun counter on each (CR 701.26a, 122.1d, 608.2b) while the third is left untouched.
# Casting it with the three Moxen leaves the pool empty in the same step.

[Bot1 Deck]
Succumb to the Cold
Mox Sapphire
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Succumb to the Cold.Cast
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#3)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Counters.Stun = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Counters.Stun = 1
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#3.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
